# guard-risk-above-threshold — a `risk >=` guard is an order, not an equality
# (§4, §6). One gate per case: a token above the threshold, one at it, one
# below. The first is the load-bearing one: every other run against a `>=`
# risk guard sits at the threshold value, where `>=` and `=` coincide.
actor  bot7
human  alice  role legal
gate   above  risk low  grant bot7
gate   at     risk low  grant bot7
gate   below  risk low  grant bot7
reserve automated_decision by legal when risk >= high
cord bot7 -> above
cord bot7 -> at
cord bot7 -> below
cord above -> master
cord at    -> master
cord below -> master
